  ('mcq-javascript-errors-and-modules-uijr5rsj7i', 'javascript', 'JavaScript, React and Node', 'errors-and-modules', null, 'A module exports let count = 0 and a function inc() that does count++. After the importer calls inc(), what does an ES module importer reading count see?', null, '[{"id":"a","text":"undefined, not exported"},{"id":"b","text":"It throws a TypeError"},{"id":"c","text":"0, a copy was taken"},{"id":"d","text":"1, it is live"}]'::jsonb, 'd', 'ES module imports are live bindings to the exporter''s variable, so the importer sees the incremented value. A CommonJS require would have given a copy of the value at the time.'),
